      r: ['Correct. Resistance means stop — forcing it can rupture the catheter or push a clot into the circulation.', 'Incorrect. That is how catheters burst.', 'Incorrect. A smaller syringe creates even higher pressure.', 'Incorrect. A drug won’t clear a blockage and may precipitate.'],
      ask: 'What can forcing a flush do?', cues: ['Resistance', 'Central line'],
